# /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-hardening.conf — Phase 3 D-19
#
# DO NOT add `Subsystem sftp ...` here — Ubuntu 24.04's main /etc/ssh/sshd_config
# already declares `Subsystem sftp`, and OpenSSH refuses to start on duplicate
# Subsystem entries (sshd: re-define for ... Subsystem → service fails to restart
# → SSH wedged). Drop-ins must NOT re-declare Subsystem; let the main config own it.
# Incident: Phase 3 / Plan 03-01 Wave 1 first-run wedged sshd on prod VPS via this
# duplicate; recovered via out-of-band console + line removal. See 03-01-SUMMARY.md
# §Carry-forward items.
PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
ChallengeResponseAuthentication no
UsePAM yes
X11Forwarding no
PrintMotd no
AcceptEnv LANG LC_*
